{%- comment -%}
  Emits the JSON array literal for schema.org `areaServed`, shared by
  kw-schema-business and kw-schema-service so the two can never disagree.

  Kilowash works in more than one state, so a flat list of place names is wrong:
  Google would read "Provo" and an Ohio town in the same unqualified array as one
  implausible service area. Instead each state is published as its own State node,
  and every place is nested under the state it actually sits in via
  `containedInPlace`. That way a name that exists in more than one state is never
  ambiguous — and several here genuinely do. "Wood County" is a real county in
  BOTH Ohio (Bowling Green, near Toledo) and West Virginia (Parkersburg); only the
  `containedInPlace` state says which one Kilowash actually drives to.

  Place lists are positional: the Nth list belongs to the Nth state named in
  `kw_seo_states_served`. Lists are optional — a blank list publishes no places for
  that state, which is the correct output for a market whose territory is not
  settled yet. The state-level claim stands on its own and nothing false is
  asserted. Supports up to three states; add a `_4` list and a `when 4` branch to
  go further.

  A place name ending in "County" is published as `AdministrativeArea`, not `City`.
  A county is not a city, and typing it as one is the kind of quiet structured-data
  lie that Google's own validator will not catch but a reviewer will.

  Place names here are stored WITHOUT a state suffix ("Washington County", not
  "Washington County OH"). The state is carried structurally by containedInPlace,
  and the visible copy in kw-service-area adds the state label for the reader.

  Usage: "areaServed": {% render 'kw-schema-areaserved' %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign state_list = settings.kw_seo_states_served | split: ','
  assign sep = ''
-%}
[
{%- for state in state_list -%}
  {%- assign state_name = state | strip -%}
  {%- if state_name != blank -%}
    {{ sep }}{ "@type": "State", "name": {{ state_name | json }} }
    {%- assign sep = ',' -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- for state in state_list -%}
  {%- assign state_name = state | strip -%}
  {%- if state_name != blank -%}
    {%- case forloop.index -%}
      {%- when 1 -%}
        {%- assign places_raw = settings.kw_seo_areas_served -%}
      {%- when 2 -%}
        {%- assign places_raw = settings.kw_seo_areas_served_2 -%}
      {%- when 3 -%}
        {%- assign places_raw = settings.kw_seo_areas_served_3 -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- assign places_raw = '' -%}
    {%- endcase -%}
    {%- assign places = places_raw | split: ',' -%}
    {%- for place in places -%}
      {%- assign place_name = place | strip -%}
      {%- if place_name != blank -%}
        {%- if place_name contains 'County' -%}
          {%- assign place_type = 'AdministrativeArea' -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- assign place_type = 'City' -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {{ sep }}{ "@type": {{ place_type | json }}, "name": {{ place_name | json }}, "containedInPlace": { "@type": "State", "name": {{ state_name | json }} } }
        {%- assign sep = ',' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
]
